# Inferring a restriction from a quoted rule
#
# Class :aaa is an OWL restriction: everything whose :bbb values are all
# :ccc. A rule in the program says exactly that of :xxx. A second rule reads
# that first rule as data, recognizes the restriction, and concludes
# :xxx a :aaa (and a rule linking :aaa back to :ccc). It shows rules that
# match other rules, and a log:query choosing what to print.

@base <https://eyereasoner.github.io/eye/reasoning/slide33/slide33.n3> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix : <http://example.org/#> .

# :aaa is the class of things whose :bbb values are all :ccc.
:aaa owl:onProperty :bbb .
:aaa owl:allValuesFrom :ccc .

# Every :bbb value of :xxx is a :ccc, so :xxx should be an :aaa.
{
    :xxx :bbb ?y .
} => {
    ?y a :ccc .
} .

# owl:allValuesFrom: when a rule says every b value of x is a c, and a is
# the restriction (b only c), conclude that x is an a, and add the rule
# "if x is an a, its b values are c".
{
    ?a owl:onProperty ?b .
    ?a owl:allValuesFrom ?c .
    {
        ?x ?b ?y .
    } => {
        ?y a ?c .
    } .
} => {
    {
        ?x a ?a .
        ?x ?b ?y .
    } => {
        ?y a ?c .
    } .
    ?x a ?a .
} .

# Print every type statement.
@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#> .

{
    ?S a ?C .
} log:query {
    ?S a ?C .
} .
